# Patches applied to the Wine tree, and what each one is.
#
#   fix        upstreamable; the goal is to send it away and delete it here
#   workaround ours to carry until upstream changes
#   debug      diagnostic only; NOT applied by default
#
# class       patch
# The dlopen/soname patches that used to live here are retracted -- see
# patches/retracted/README.md. bin/bundle-libs plus soname seeding in
# bin/build-runtime replaces all of them.
workaround    wine-0004-kernelbase-append-args-env.patch
debug         wine-0005-winemac-surface-flush-trace.patch
# Rosetta 2 loses the CS change on the WoW64 far ljmp, so 32-bit PE processes die
# in an unrecoverable exception-delivery loop. Ported from CrossOver's CW HACK
# 20760; gated on the VirtualApple brand string, so inert on real x86_64.
# Without this, NO 32-bit game can be relied on. See docs/NEXT.md.
workaround    wine-0006-wow64cpu-rosetta2-mode-switch.patch
# Synchronous WM_NCPAINT blocked the painting thread, making 2D/GDI menus take
# 5-10 s per hover. Ported from CrossOver's CW Hack 20969/23427. The paired
# WM_ERASEBKGND bound (23394) is carried too, but measured ZERO hits -- it is a
# diagnostic, not the fix. See docs/NEXT.md.
workaround    wine-0007-win32u-async-ncpaint.patch
# CW Hack 24834 port, extracted from src/wine where an earlier session had applied
# it with no patch file at all -- so build-runtime silently dropped it. Inert
# unless WINEMAC_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX=1.
workaround    wine-0008-winemac-forward-compat-gl-context.patch

# NOTE (2026-07-30): 0006, 0007 and 0008 are all ports of CrossOver hacks, and
# 0004 is a workaround for something CrossOver fixes properly (CX HACK 23950).
# All four become redundant once the tree is rebased onto CrossOver's Wine --
# see docs/NEXT.md, "The pivot". They are kept until that rebase lands so the
# game keeps working in the meantime.
#
# 0005 is class `debug`, so build-runtime skips it -- but it is ALREADY APPLIED in
# src/wine, which makes the skip meaningless and ships trace code in the surface
# flush path. Revert it in src/wine, or reclassify it. Not yet decided.

# DXMT (built separately, see backends/)
fix           dxmt-0001-include-iomanip.patch
